WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.144 --> 00:00:03.567
-My next guest is already
a Critics' Choice Award winner

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:06.567
who stars in a film
that's nominated for six Oscars,

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:08.300
and he's only 8 years old.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.367
From "Minari," which is
currently available in theaters,

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.968
on A24 Screening Room,
and on demand,

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:16.067
pease welcome Alan Kim!

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:17.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:20.067
Hey, buddy!
Oh! [ Laughs ]

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:23.100
Wow. How you doing, buddy?
Welcome to the show.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.667
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:28.133
-Thank you.
I'm so glad to be here.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.167
[ Audience awws ]
-Are you kidding me?

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:32.300
Stop it. This is...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.868
Now, buddy, you're
8 years old -- am I correct?

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.868
-Yes.
It's April 9th right now.

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:44.167
So, in around 14 days,
I'm turning 9.

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.067
-Oh! Well, happy early birthday!

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:47.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.434
-Thank you.

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:50.901
-What do you want
for your birthday?

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:53.300
Do you know?

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.467
-What I want for my birthday...

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:59.300
That's a hard one.
-It is?

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.434
-Um, well, definitely not
another hoverboard.

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:07.367
-You -- You don't --
You already have a hoverboard?

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.767
-Yes.
-Oh.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.033
-I do.
-I love hoverboards.

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:13.667
-Well, then...
yeah, I guess a new bike.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:16.534
-A new bike? Yeah?
You need a new one?

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:18.067
-Yeah.
My old one...

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:19.067
[ Clicks tongue ]

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:22.534
...the chain keeps falling off.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.868
-[ Laughs ]
Yeah, get a new one there.

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:27.267
Are you going to --
Are you going to celebrate,

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.667
have a cake and all that stuff?

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:33.067
-Well, we were thinking
to going to Boomers!

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:37.234
but [breathes sharply]
it closes on weekdays, so...

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:38.667
[ Audience awws ]

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:39.667
-Are you kidding me
with this kid?

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:41.133
Oh, my God.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:42.467
What is Boomers!?

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.100
And we could probably make sure
they open for you.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.200
What's Boomers!?
What is Boomers!?

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.000
-Well, Boomers! -- it's a --

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.968
kind of like Chuck E. Cheese
or Dave &amp; Buster's.

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:57.033
-Yeah!
-Except it has, like, rides.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.467
-Oh, wow.

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:03.434
-And like a miniature version
of only the rides at Disneyland.

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.367
-Wow! That's --
Are you scared to go on rides,

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:07.801
or you're cool with those?

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:10.467
-No.
I'm cool with those.

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:14.434
I just, like, don't like --
like, I went to Boomers!

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.834
like, on Wednesday,

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:18.467
and I [breathes sharply] --

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:23.934
I went to one ride,
and that had a water fountain.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:26.834
And I went through that,
and I got drenched.

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:28.501
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. You got wet.

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:30.567
I -- You know, I --
I have a ride --

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.934
if you ever go
to Orlando, Florida,

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:36.968
I actually have a roller coaster
at the Universal theme park.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:39.501
-Oh, wow!
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:42.000
You got to go on that.
You will not get wet.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.133
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:46.968
-Hey, I want to talk about
your movie, if you don't mind --

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:49.901
"Minari."
Congratulations on this.

00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:51.434
Winning the award
is unbelievable,

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:53.601
and you -- great performance.

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:54.834
Can you tell us, everyone,

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:56.501
what the movie is about --
"Minari"?

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:59.868
-Well, "Minari" is
about a Korean-American family

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:02.133
that moves to Arkansas

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:05.634
to get a better living
than they did in California.

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:08.567
And the grandma comes
to babysit the children

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:11.200
while the parents
are away at work.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.834
-Yeah.
-But David, my character,

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:17.501
doesn't like the grandma
at first.

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:20.767
But throughout the movie,
she starts growing on him.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.100
-Yeah.
She's really funny,

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.601
and you're really funny
in the movie, too.

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:25.734
Did you enjoy making it?

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:28.701
Did you have fun making it?
-Yeah.

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:31.133
Especially the pee scene.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.067
That was really funny.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.701
-Well, no spoilers, but, yeah,

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:37.000
so, that was a good --
that was a good scene, as well.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.868
I want to say congratulations
on everything.

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:41.033
And, man, oh, man,
you couldn't be more charming.

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:43.033
Happy early birthday.
Have fun at Boomers!

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:44.934
Tell 'em all I said, "Hi,"
please.

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:47.400
-[ Chuckles ] Thank you.
-Yeah, bud.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:52.200
Here's Alan Kim in "Minari."

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.801
Take a look.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.901
-[ Speaking Korean ]

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:08.734
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:18.934
-Pretty boy, pretty boy!

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:21.033
Pretty --
-I'm not pretty!

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:22.400
I'm good-looking!

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.767
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:27.400
-That's what I'm talking
about right there, buddy!

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.634
-Yep!
-Alan Kim!

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.767
Please come back, buddy,
whenever you can.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:31.968
You're more than welcome back.

